@matte21 is the testcase literally just adding this to delta_fifo_test.go?

```
func TestDeltaFIFO_ReplaceOverridesDeletions(t *testing.T) {
	f := NewDeltaFIFO(
		testFifoObjectKeyFunc,
		keyLookupFunc(func() []testFifoObject {
			return []testFifoObject{mkFifoObj("baz", 10)}
		}),
	)
	f.Delete(mkFifoObj("baz", 10))
	f.Replace([]interface{}{mkFifoObj("baz", 5)}, "0")

	expectedList := []Deltas{
		// A Replace()-generated Sync should always be enqueued even if
		// there is an existing Deleted delta. This ensures that a new
		// object with the same key as the deleted one is not ignored.
		{{Deleted, mkFifoObj("baz", 10)}},
		{{Sync, mkFifoObj("baz", 5)}},
	}

	for _, expected := range expectedList {
		cur := Pop(f).(Deltas)
		if e, a := expected, cur; !reflect.DeepEqual(e, a) {
			t.Errorf("Expected %#v, got %#v", e, a)
		}
	}
}
```

But for some reason this hangs in the Pop(f).

> How about this change ?

@tedyu DeltaFIFO only de-dupes deletions, but your example would do effectively extend that to compressing Delete+Sync=Sync. You used to be able to build smarter compression off DeltaFIFO (eg https://github.com/openshift/origin/pull/10070/files#diff-0220ccb2c017c89846fc17ff28c57837R176 ) but nobody actually used the DeltaCompressor stuff so we removed it. And nobody above DeltaFIFO expects compressed events now :(

In your example I'd be a bit worried about the implications of not deleting the object, since the Sync-ed one probably has a different UUID and thus technically not be the same object as the deleted one. Might not be a big issue, but this is critical path code so I'd personally rather be a bit conservative.

> I agree about not compressing. I do wonder if a sync arriving on top of a delete should turn into an Added event (in at least one path, like the one described in this issue, that is exactly what happens).

@liggitt if this happens, I think it should happen on top of the DeltaFIFO, not in the DF. Let's keep DF simpler since it's (a) complicated enough and (b) critical path code.

> It's a little hard to reason about what this sync event should be when we know that relists can currently time-travel backwards.
> 
> Edit: it looks like shared informer code will [turn the Sync event into an Added event](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/staging/src/k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/shared_informer.go#L456-L468) if it follows a delete event.

@liggitt probably the right place for compression, if any happens. IMHO it's correct that Deletes don't get compressed, eg that Delete + Add is not compressed into Update or something like that.
